WEBVTT

00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:05.179
(loud gasp)

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.749
-EDITH: Wow! This is so cool!
-AGNES: Look at that!

00:00:07.782 --> 00:00:09.851
Oh, my gosh,
he's even got a helicopter!

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:11.720
AGNES:
This the best!

00:00:11.753 --> 00:00:13.187
Yes, the best!

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:14.856
(quietly): All right,
let's go home now.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:16.524
Home? Why?

00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:20.194
I don't know. This guy
with the mansion and the cars,

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:22.697
and all of the hair,
with the silky smooth,

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:24.866
luxurious... hair.

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:27.301
I feel worse
than I did before I came.

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:28.703
Oh, but he's your brother, Gru.

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.438
-Give this a chance.
-DRU: Oh.

00:00:30.471 --> 00:00:33.742
I was thinking, while Gru and I
catch up on some brother stuff,

00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:35.143
you girls should go
with Fritz.

00:00:35.176 --> 00:00:36.477
He has a surprise for you.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.746
-Yay! -Yay!
-Awesome!

00:00:37.779 --> 00:00:39.380
I love surprises!

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:40.782
Oh, this is perfect!
Mother-daughter

00:00:40.815 --> 00:00:43.284
bonding time.
Let's do it! (whoops)

00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:45.720
-(laughter)
-Bye! You boys have fun!

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:49.457
Ah, ha, ha. Whoopee!

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.425
(upbeat TV commercial
music plays)

00:00:51.459 --> 00:00:54.462
ANNOUNCER: Now you can be
as evil as Balthazar Bratt

00:00:54.495 --> 00:00:56.397
with the Evil Bratt
action figure.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.267
Featuring music-activated
break dance mode.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.835
Also featuring

00:01:00.869 --> 00:01:04.773
bubblegum-launching
shoulder pads!

00:01:04.806 --> 00:01:08.142
And the all-new
Mega Diamond Laser!

00:01:09.844 --> 00:01:11.746
No more math!

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.483
I've been a bad boy!
(cackling)

00:01:15.516 --> 00:01:16.918
ANNOUNCER:
Mega Diamond Laser

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:18.486
does not actually
incinerate books.

00:01:18.519 --> 00:01:21.089
(sighs) How could Hollywood
cancel a show

00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:23.591
that produced toys
like this, Clive?

00:01:23.624 --> 00:01:26.928
Evil Bratt was a masterpiece!

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:29.664
Does no one value
true art anymore?

00:01:29.698 --> 00:01:32.033
It's a disgrace
and a travesty, sir.

00:01:32.066 --> 00:01:35.804
Well, now that I've got
the diamond, it's payback time.

00:01:35.837 --> 00:01:39.540
Oh, it's too bad Gru won't be
around to try and stop me.

00:01:39.573 --> 00:01:41.009
Oh, wait!
No, it's not.

00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:42.476
I hate that dweeb!

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.145
And you, Hollywood!

00:01:44.178 --> 00:01:47.348
This time,
I'm canceling you...

00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:50.218
and all the losers
who rejected me!

00:01:50.251 --> 00:01:52.353
-(loud whirring)
-(cackling)

00:01:55.423 --> 00:01:57.792
Oh, piggy, piggy!

00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:01.295
So, how are things going
for you career-wise?

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:03.031
(laughing):
Great!

00:02:03.064 --> 00:02:04.532
So, so, great!

00:02:04.565 --> 00:02:06.067
Crushing it.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.636
Well, I've got something
that I think

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:11.940
-you will find
very interesting. -(squeals)

00:02:13.742 --> 00:02:16.177
-(beeps) -Hold onto your face,
brother. (chuckling)

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.579
(whirring, thud)

00:02:18.612 --> 00:02:21.249
(thudding)

00:02:21.282 --> 00:02:22.683
(both yelling)

00:02:22.717 --> 00:02:25.987
Yee-haw! Ya! Ya!

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.655
Aah! Ya.

00:02:27.688 --> 00:02:31.059
-(squealing) -(chattering,
whimpering, yelling)

00:02:31.092 --> 00:02:32.994
(yelling)

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:34.428
(whimpering)

00:02:34.462 --> 00:02:36.564
-Ow.
-(yell)

00:02:36.597 --> 00:02:38.833
Ooh. Ah. Sunny.

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:40.234
(yells)

00:02:40.268 --> 00:02:41.602
Hey. (speaks Minionese)
Sunny.

00:02:41.635 --> 00:02:43.571
Ah. Sí, sí.
(muffled chatter)

00:02:43.604 --> 00:02:45.206
-Uh, Sunny.
-(squawks)

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:47.909
-Oh. Oh. Oh!
-Come. Come on!

00:02:47.942 --> 00:02:49.443
(laughing)

00:02:49.477 --> 00:02:52.546
(gasps)
What is all this?

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.749
DRU:
The pig farm was just a cover

00:02:54.783 --> 00:02:57.886
for the real family business.

00:02:57.919 --> 00:02:59.553
Uh.

00:02:59.587 --> 00:03:01.189
(giggles)
Hey. (speaking Minionese)

00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:03.257
-And boobs.
-(laughs)

00:03:03.291 --> 00:03:07.628
Now, feast your eyes on...

00:03:07.661 --> 00:03:10.631
Dad's lair!

00:03:10.664 --> 00:03:12.633
Tada! (laughs)

00:03:12.666 --> 00:03:15.436
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait.

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:18.306
So, our dad was a villain?

00:03:18.339 --> 00:03:20.708
No, no, no,
not just a villain.

00:03:20.741 --> 00:03:24.412
One of the greatest
of all time!

00:03:24.445 --> 00:03:28.950
He was known
as "The Bald Terror."

00:03:28.983 --> 00:03:30.251
That's him?

00:03:30.284 --> 00:03:31.886
Our dad?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.654
He was so proud of you

00:03:33.687 --> 00:03:35.589
and what a great villain
you were.

00:03:35.623 --> 00:03:37.258
(gasps)
He was?

00:03:37.291 --> 00:03:40.661
But me, ah,
uh, not so much.

00:03:40.694 --> 00:03:43.431
To Dad... I was...

00:03:43.464 --> 00:03:46.300
just a... failure.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:49.603
He never thought I had
what it took to be a villain.

00:03:49.637 --> 00:03:52.841
But now, you can help me
prove him wrong!

00:03:52.874 --> 00:03:55.409
Brother...

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:58.746
teach me the art of villainy!

00:03:58.779 --> 00:04:00.781
No.

00:04:00.815 --> 00:04:02.984
No, no, no,
I can't do that.

00:04:03.017 --> 00:04:04.418
What? But it...

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:05.954
it's our family tradition!

00:04:05.987 --> 00:04:07.521
You can't say no to that!

00:04:07.555 --> 00:04:09.657
Look, I'm sorry.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.793
I left that life behind me.
End of story.

00:04:12.827 --> 00:04:15.496
Oh. O-Okay.

00:04:15.529 --> 00:04:17.465
I understand.

00:04:17.498 --> 00:04:20.301
Hmm. I wonder what this does.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:23.104
(muttering,
whimpering)

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:25.573
(yelling)

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.019
Holy moley!

00:04:38.052 --> 00:04:40.188
Dad's villain wheels!

00:04:40.221 --> 00:04:42.356
Pretty slick, huh?

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:45.226
Hey, you want
to take her out for a spin?

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:47.695
Just for some fun?

00:04:47.728 --> 00:04:50.999
Mm...

00:04:51.032 --> 00:04:54.468
DRU:
Whoo-hoo-hoo...!

00:04:54.502 --> 00:04:57.071
GRU: Oh! Oh! Oh!
Look out! Whoa, whoa!

00:04:57.105 --> 00:04:59.407
Whoa! Whoa, whoa!
Whoa, whoa! Oh!

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.574
Ha-ha!

00:05:00.608 --> 00:05:02.510
What a beautiful day!

00:05:02.543 --> 00:05:05.346
Zero to 400 in three seconds.

00:05:05.379 --> 00:05:07.148
Able to withstand
a nuclear blast.

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:08.682
Armed to the teeth!

00:05:08.716 --> 00:05:10.818
Oh-ho-ho!

00:05:10.851 --> 00:05:12.720
Okay, that's pretty nice.

00:05:12.753 --> 00:05:15.223
-And it's a hybrid.
-Oh, look out!

00:05:16.557 --> 00:05:18.826
Aah!

00:05:18.859 --> 00:05:21.896
-* Do it all again
-(both screaming)

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.564
-* Whoo, ooh
-* Come on, now

00:05:23.597 --> 00:05:24.999
* Whoo, ooh

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.867
-* Come on, now, whoo, ooh
-(screaming continues)

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.336
(screaming stops)

00:05:28.369 --> 00:05:30.504
* Some did not believe
that you could *

00:05:30.538 --> 00:05:33.107
(gasping)

00:05:34.575 --> 00:05:36.244
Wah-wah-wah-wah-wah!

00:05:36.277 --> 00:05:38.712
-(screaming)
-* Some did not believe

00:05:38.746 --> 00:05:40.281
Help me!

00:05:40.314 --> 00:05:42.116
Whoa! Ooh!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.453
(vibrating):
I am not enjoying this...!

00:05:45.486 --> 00:05:47.088
Aah!

00:05:47.121 --> 00:05:50.224
-Ooh!
-(Dru cackles, whoops)

00:05:51.325 --> 00:05:55.096
(men singing lively song)

00:05:55.129 --> 00:05:57.465
Whoa! What is going on here?

00:05:57.498 --> 00:06:01.402
Welcome to the annual
Freedonian Cheese Festival.

00:06:01.435 --> 00:06:03.104
GAME HOST:
Go!

00:06:03.137 --> 00:06:04.672
(cheering)

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.111
(gasps) Oh, look! Look!
Look at all the candies!

00:06:10.144 --> 00:06:11.980
-(giggles)
-Whoa-hoa-hoa!

00:06:12.013 --> 00:06:13.814
(imitating chicks peeping)

00:06:13.847 --> 00:06:15.549
-Lucy, can we get these?
-Please?

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:17.551
(sighs)
Okay, but only one each.

00:06:17.585 --> 00:06:19.120
I mean it.

00:06:19.153 --> 00:06:20.821
-Aw.
-Aw, man.

00:06:20.854 --> 00:06:22.090
No, I don't. (laughs)

00:06:22.123 --> 00:06:24.125
Get as many as you want.
I don't care.

00:06:24.158 --> 00:06:26.060
-Whoo-hoo!
-Yay! Awesome!

00:06:26.094 --> 00:06:27.328
-Uh...
-What?

00:06:27.361 --> 00:06:30.664
Well, it's okay
to tell them no sometimes, too.

00:06:30.698 --> 00:06:32.800
You know?
Moms need to be tough.

00:06:32.833 --> 00:06:34.802
Right, right. Tough. Good one.

00:06:34.835 --> 00:06:36.437
I can totally do that.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:38.639
You know, still figuring out
this mom thing.

00:06:38.672 --> 00:06:41.342
-Gettin' my sea legs, matey.
-(Agnes yells)

00:06:41.375 --> 00:06:43.244
It's a unicorn!

00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:45.213
*

00:06:47.815 --> 00:06:48.983
Can we go in there?

00:06:49.017 --> 00:06:51.319
Please, please, please,
please, please?

00:06:51.352 --> 00:06:52.953
(grunting, snorting)

00:06:52.987 --> 00:06:55.256
Um... yeah, sure, yeah.

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:57.025
You know,
but first let's, um...

00:06:57.058 --> 00:06:58.792
(gasps)
Oh, look!

00:06:58.826 --> 00:07:00.961
LUCY: It's a traditional
Freedonian dance.

00:07:00.995 --> 00:07:02.963
How amazing does that look?

00:07:02.997 --> 00:07:05.799
ALL:
* Say, say, say cheese!

00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:08.169
Cheese! I love this.

00:07:08.202 --> 00:07:10.504
LUCY: The little girls go
and get the cheese

00:07:10.538 --> 00:07:11.939
from the little boys.

00:07:11.972 --> 00:07:14.042
Oh, that's adorable!

00:07:14.075 --> 00:07:16.010
-*
-(girl giggles)

00:07:16.044 --> 00:07:18.379
Aw, look at that
poor little guy.

00:07:18.412 --> 00:07:19.980
-With his little boots.
-(boots squeaking)

00:07:20.014 --> 00:07:21.982
Nobody picked him.

00:07:22.016 --> 00:07:24.618
Oh. Margo,
why-why don't you go up there?

00:07:24.652 --> 00:07:26.720
-No way.
-Okay.

00:07:26.754 --> 00:07:28.322
Wait a minute.

00:07:28.356 --> 00:07:31.559
No. Go take a bite
of his cheese, young lady,

00:07:31.592 --> 00:07:33.461
right now.

00:07:33.494 --> 00:07:36.330
-What? -I'm being tougher.
You know, like you said.

00:07:36.364 --> 00:07:38.299
No, I-I meant
be tougher on them.

00:07:38.332 --> 00:07:39.567
Not me.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.001
Oh, come on, just do it.

00:07:41.035 --> 00:07:42.636
What's the worst
that could happen?

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.206
-(quietly): Mm.
-(boots squeaking)

00:07:45.239 --> 00:07:46.707
Fine.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.209
(gasps)

00:07:48.242 --> 00:07:49.643
(trembles)

00:07:49.677 --> 00:07:53.414
-(birds chirping)
-NIKO: Wow!

00:07:53.447 --> 00:07:56.016
Hey there. I'm Margo.

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.751
Hello, Margo!

00:07:57.785 --> 00:07:59.520
I-I am Niko.

00:07:59.553 --> 00:08:03.191
Would you like
some of my cheese?

00:08:03.224 --> 00:08:05.393
-Mmm! -PEOPLE: * Say, say,
say cheese! *

00:08:05.426 --> 00:08:07.861
Yes! Yes! Yes! Thank you,
Margo! Thank you!

00:08:07.895 --> 00:08:09.863
Whoo-ha-ha-hey!

00:08:09.897 --> 00:08:11.699
-Bam! I am a great mother.
-* Say, say, say cheese!

00:08:11.732 --> 00:08:13.434
(chuckles)
Did you see that, girls?

00:08:13.467 --> 00:08:15.503
I laid down the...

00:08:15.536 --> 00:08:18.072
LUCY:
Oh, no. Where are they?

00:08:18.106 --> 00:08:20.808
Ooh, Agnes? Edith!

